To implement the 0/1 knapsack, you can use a 1D DP array where dp[w] represents the maximum value that can be achieved with a weight limit of w. Start from the back of the array to prevent overwriting values that are still needed. Here’s an example:

def knapsack(weights, values, capacity):
    dp = [0] * (capacity + 1)
    for i in range(len(weights)):
        for w in range(capacity, weights[i] - 1, -1):
            dp[w] = max(dp[w], dp[w - weights[i]] + values[i])
    return dp[capacity]

